WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:10.680
Rhett: Due to a large influx of fake weapons, we had to redo this beautiful weapon rack wall that we've had.

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:13.720
It's gonna go across down here.

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:16.940
We're gonna do a second rack across here.

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:21.960
And then we're gonna save this piece of board and shift it up and over for some of the other items.

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:25.060
It's gonna fit a whole lot more of 'em.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:29.440
*weapon breaks*

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:30.860
Wren: *Pffffff*

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:34.780
Don't put that in the edit!

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:47.800
Now I'm pulling incredibly large nails, that have been hammered over like crazy,

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:51.300
back out of these boards because we recycle.

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:52.200
Cmike: Oh no!

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:54.380
Wren, help!

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:55.680
Wren: Oh, I'm coming.

00:00:57.340 --> 00:01:00.140
Always here to clean up your mess, Carmichael!

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:03.080
So, no idea what's in this. Let's find out.

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:03.800
I don't-

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:06.860
Oh my god! Are you serious?!

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:10.480
This is one of those portable gaming sets, you put your console in here.

00:01:10.480 --> 00:01:12.440
Was this just like sitting in here?!

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:13.480
Cmike: There's another one right there.

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:17.940
I assume this will work just fine with a PS4 or something.

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:21.420
Is there like a battery or do you have to plug it into power?

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:22.940
If I were to ask Niko about it he'd probably be like

00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:24.200
"Oh yeah. Yeah, we've had that."

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:26.740
Do you know- do you know what these are?

00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:32.560
Niko: Yeah they're suitcases that are supposed to fit an Xbox and they come with a screen inside.

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:33.600
Wren: How long have we had these?

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:34.720
Niko: They've been upstairs for years.

00:01:35.800 --> 00:01:36.680
I don't know.

00:01:36.680 --> 00:01:42.060
It turns out, you know, we hook our Xboxes up to TVs and don't use them for mobile gaming.

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:43.760
Wren: That's what phones are for.

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:45.720
Okay, yeah so you do plug this into power.

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:48.040
Niko: Yeah it needs to be plugged in so it's kinda useless.

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:49.940
It does have a cool little HDMI cable, though.

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:52.720
Wren: This is probably more useful than anything else in this.

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:54.840
Treasure, yeah, found it.

